You can have a class for your dialogues. For example, when the player talks to an NPC, you can call a method that presents the options and handles the player's choice. Here's a simple example:
public class Dialogue {
    private String[] options;
    private String[] responses;

    public Dialogue(String[] options, String[] responses) {
        this.options = options;
        this.responses = responses;
    }

    public void start() {
        for (int i = 0; i < options.length; i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ". " + options[i]);
        }

        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        int choice = scanner.nextInt();

        if (choice >= 1 && choice <= options.length) {
            System.out.println(responses[choice - 1]);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Invalid choice.");
        }
    }
}

